rain dependence of the fine-structure constant on gravitational environment, including scalar-mediated behavior inaccessible to small seasonal potential changes near Earth?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b6f59ba7e7bc46f5552b8741f188a8c1fb7803d445c34db63465d2208faacc04","title":"What physical fields and interactions result when a real scalar gauge field B accompanies the usual U(1) vector gauge field, particularly after a charged complex scalar develops a vacuum expectation value?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0015"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b6f16126a8df0660481b3e9a274dffa137a4396f76b43e99033ca07ca0a3e36e","title":"Can axion–four-form monodromy sustain approximately quadratic, large-field inflation in a high-scale string setting, and can nearby UV scales produce observable corrections without destabilizing inflation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0016"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b648f093f0244ce95e455b8efad3bb085b689ddc1b9e2cf70820ab0dfb001ed3","title":"Can the Taub–NUT uplift of a D6 system support a localized, stationary BGHHS charge? The problem reduces the three-form fluctuation to a radial equation for g=F²Q.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b638d7f3c7687a6235089349414d265455db69014eeacf5958c538af1c8b4a23","title":"How do the genuine electric, magnetic and dyonic line operators, theta-angle identifications and electromagnetic charges depend on the Standard Model's global gauge group G = [U(1) × SU(2) × SU(3)]/Γ, with Γ = 1, Z2, Z3 or Z6?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b655e6e53aea7fa9771e9113247ce896ea19588ee8fa058e4e4bbc42666dab3a