hdrawn.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0067"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b60872edddbe3fb02cbe7c5963d5decb80a66807ee85479edd684486bccb6d19","title":"How can infinite-distance complex-structure degenerations of elliptic K3 surfaces be classified through canonical Weierstrass models, and how does this geometry support their F-theory interpretation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0070"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b68acd3b7e8bbb6ca8616a434ba51647462d4a74c4b5b0973b844abddf21146d","title":"Which geometric and spectral conditions connect the local Tower Scalar Weak Gravity Conjecture to the asymptotic Sharpened Distance Conjecture when moduli spaces are curved and scalar-charge-to-mass vectors vary with moduli?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0083"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b6b50ab7acba6600bb86c0579297898af67e7c4f312f81c2a0e9be65eff94669","title":"How do apparently O(s^3) matter-annihilation amplitudes producing longitudinal massive KK gravitons cancel, what geometric identities enforce this, and how does stabilization change the analysis?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0084"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b6327667ae3d048cd2b81005de30206c8a6d2cd3c2165861868d2e348c86ecb3","title":"Can the one-loop potential uplift non-supersymmetric O(16) × O(16) heterotic AdS3 × S3 × T4 vacua to de Sitter, and which gravitational and torus-modulus fluctuations remain perturbatively stable?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0097"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:b6ba9366d5236b8db613a047e515ef2bfa7fa8a6719f021dad87e4b088456375","title":"Does M-theory on finite-volume K3×T² provide the superextremal particle towers required by the minimal WGC in extreme coupling limits, and 